# Optional — enables real Claude vision analysis and AI designer narratives.
# Without it, Maison runs in deterministic demo mode (sample rooms are fully
# functional; uploaded photos get a simulated analysis).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional — enables the live VidaXL/DropshippingXL dropship feed at
# /suppliers. Without all three set, that page falls back to a realistic
# mock feed so the ingestion pipeline (see lib/suppliers/) is testable
# before real credentials exist.
#
# VIDAXL_API_URL: base URL only, no path — use the sandbox first
# (request access via support@dropXL.com) before pointing at prod:
#   sandbox: https://sandbox.b2b.dropxl.com
#   prod:    https://b2b.dropxl.com
# VIDAXL_ACCOUNT_EMAIL: the email your DropshippingXL account is registered
# with — required alongside the token because their API uses HTTP Basic
# auth (email:token), not a bearer token.
# VIDAXL_API_KEY: the API token generated in your DropshippingXL dashboard.
VIDAXL_API_URL=
VIDAXL_ACCOUNT_EMAIL=
VIDAXL_API_KEY=

# Optional — enables the GPT-Image compositing step (lib/ai/composite.ts):
# inserting a real product photo into a real room photo via a masked edit,
# and (with ANTHROPIC_API_KEY also set) removing furniture already
# physically in a room photo (lib/ai/locate.ts + removeExistingObject —
# no separate provider needed for that). Separate account/billing from
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY — Claude has no image generation/editing capability,
# this specifically needs OpenAI. Real cost per call (roughly $0.01–$0.03
# /image at low/medium quality with gpt-image-1.5 at time of writing —
# confirm current pricing yourself, this isn't guaranteed to stay
# accurate). Adding a product (compositeProductIntoRoom, called from
# app/api/composite) uses "high" quality specifically — a real, confirmed
# test showed "medium" still under-rendered product detail (missing arms,
# wrong cushion count) even with a correctly-shaped mask and a clean
# reference photo, so "high" costs meaningfully more than the low/medium
# range above; removal (removeExistingObject) stays on "low".
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional — enables Postgres persistence (lib/db.ts): rooms, chat history,
# constraints and rendered versions survive a refresh instead of living only
# in the browser tab. A Neon connection string works as-is (the driver is
# @neondatabase/serverless); any standard Postgres connection string should
# work too. Without this, the Designer Agent still works, just stateless.
# After setting this, run `npx tsx scripts/seed-products.ts` once to load
# the catalog into Postgres (otherwise search falls back to the live feed).
DATABASE_URL=

# Optional — enables transactional email (lib/email.ts): magic-link login
# and order confirmations. Get a key at resend.com (free tier is generous
# for a new store). Without it, emails are logged to the server console
# instead of sent — login/order flows still work, just with no email
# actually delivered, so set this before real customers sign up.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Optional — the "From" address on outgoing email, e.g. "Maison <hello@yourdomain.tld>".
# Requires verifying that sending domain in Resend's dashboard first.
# Without this, falls back to Resend's own onboarding@resend.dev sandbox
# address, which only delivers to the Resend account's own verified email —
# fine for testing, not for real customers.
EMAIL_FROM=

# Optional — enables real payment collection: one-time furniture checkout
# (lib/stripe.ts, app/api/checkout/session) AND the Premium subscription
# checkout (app/api/checkout/premium — unlimited AI generations, bypassing
# the credit system in lib/credits.ts). Get this from the
# Stripe dashboard (use a test-mode "sk_test_..." key while developing,
# switch to a live "sk_live_..." key only when you're ready to take real
# payments/subscriptions). Without it (or without DATABASE_URL, since we
# need somewhere to record the order/account), furniture checkout falls
# back to an instant demo confirmation with no real charge, and Premium
# checkout returns 501. The Premium price (currently CHF 19/month) is
# defined inline in that route, not a pre-created Stripe Price ID — no
# separate dashboard setup needed for it beyond this one key.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=

# Required alongside STRIPE_SECRET_KEY for the webhook (app/api/webhooks/stripe)
# to trust incoming events. Get this by creating a webhook endpoint in the
# Stripe dashboard pointed at https://yourdomain.tld/api/webhooks/stripe,
# subscribed to "checkout.session.completed", "customer.subscription.updated",
# and "customer.subscription.deleted" (the last two turn Premium back off
# when a subscription lapses or is canceled) — Stripe shows you the signing
# secret ("whsec_...") once the endpoint is created. Without this, the
# webhook route refuses all events rather than trusting unverified ones.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# No env var needed for the credit system (lib/credits.ts) — it's always
# on. Every anonymous session starts with FREE_CREDITS (currently 3) AI
# room generations; each confirmed render spends one. Premium accounts
# (STRIPE_SECRET_KEY above) bypass it entirely. To grant/reset credits on
# your own session while testing locally, hit /api/debug/credits (GET for
# balance + history, POST {action:"grant"|"reset", amount} to adjust) —
# disabled outside development.

# Optional — enables Replicate-hosted models, gated behind this one token.
# Currently used for ONE thing: existing-furniture removal
# (lib/ai/fluxFill.ts's removeExistingObjectFlux*) stays the primary
# removal path when this is set — Grounded-SAM segmentation (lib/ai/vision/
# segmentation.ts) + FLUX Fill erase, more precise than OpenAI's box-only
# removal. OpenAI stays the automatic fallback when this isn't set.
# Real bug fixed here: segmentation.ts was reading the wrong entry out of
# the model's output array (the annotated visualization image instead of
# the actual binary mask at index 2) — confirmed via a real garbled
# removal render (hallucinated content smeared well outside the removed
# object) before the fix. Fixed now; retest removal if you saw that.
#
# Adding a product (lib/ai/composite.ts's compositeProductIntoRoom) does
# NOT use this at all — it's OpenAI-only, and as of the latest change is
# an UNMASKED full-image edit (no mask sent to OpenAI, no local blend-back)
# rather than a masked region — every masked-edit variant tried, including
# a segmentation-refined blend-back mask via this Replicate token, produced
# its own real failure, so masking was dropped from that path entirely
# rather than layering another fix on top.
#
# Setting this adds a real extra Replicate call (cost + latency, roughly
# another 5-15s) on top of removal's OpenAI/FLUX cost — get a token at
# replicate.com/account/api-tokens, billed separately from OpenAI/
# Anthropic. Check current pricing for black-forest-labs/flux-fill-pro and
# schananas/grounded_sam yourself before relying on this in front of real
# customers.
REPLICATE_API_TOKEN=

# Optional overrides for the exact Replicate model slug used — see the
# module doc comments in lib/ai/vision/segmentation.ts and lib/ai/fluxFill.ts
# for why these are env vars rather than hardcoded: Replicate model
# availability drifts, and the site blocks automated verification, so the
# defaults below are the best-verified choice at the time this was written,
# not a guarantee they're still current or optimal by the time you read
# this. Leave unset to use the defaults (schananas/grounded_sam and
# black-forest-labs/flux-fill-pro).
REPLICATE_SEGMENTATION_MODEL=
REPLICATE_FLUX_MODEL=

# Optional — enables SerpApi's Google Shopping search
# (lib/suppliers/serpApiSearch.ts) as the primary "not in our catalog"
# product search (the poster/art-print gap case) — structured JSON results
# with a direct image URL, no page-scraping. Without this, that fallback
# uses the existing Claude-agentic web search instead (slower, and a
# confirmed-unreliable page-scraping approach for finding a usable product
# photo — see lib/ai/webProductSearch.ts). Get a key at serpapi.com (free
# tier: ~100 searches/month).
SERPAPI_KEY=

# ── Ad conversion tracking (Meta Pixel + Google Ads) ─────────────────────
# Optional, and consent-gated regardless: components/TrackingScripts.tsx
# only loads these AFTER a visitor accepts the cookie banner
# (components/ConsentBanner.tsx). Setting these keys does not track anyone
# who hasn't opted in — see app/legal/privacy/page.tsx clause 4, which was
# rewritten specifically to disclose this honestly rather than leaving it
# to be discovered.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix is required — these are read in the BROWSER, not on
# the server, so anything here ends up in the client JS bundle. Never put
# a real secret in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable; these pixel/ads IDs are public
# identifiers by design (they appear in your page source either way), not
# credentials.
#
# Meta Pixel ID — Events Manager > Data Sources > your Pixel > Settings.
NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=
# Google Ads conversion ID, format "AW-XXXXXXXXXX" — Google Ads > Goals >
# Conversions > your conversion action > "Google tag" setup.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ADS_ID=
# The conversion action's label (the part after the slash in "AW-XXX/YYY"
# on the same setup screen) — required for the Purchase event specifically;
# without it gtag still loads (page-view tracking works) but no purchase
# conversion fires.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ADS_PURCHASE_LABEL=

# ── AliExpress (accent items, preferred over CJ) ─────────────────────────
# Unlike CJ, a single API key is NOT enough: the Alibaba open-platform
# gateway signs every request, so you need an App Key AND an App Secret.
# Register an app at openservice.aliexpress.com and enable the Affiliate
# API — that is the surface which permits product search. The Dropshipping
# (DS) API needs an approved partner account and OAuth on top.
#
# Verify with:  npx tsx scripts/aliexpress-test-fetch.ts "rgb led strip"
# That probe prints the gateway's own error text, which is what
# distinguishes a wrong signature from an unapproved app.
ALIEXPRESS_APP_KEY=
ALIEXPRESS_APP_SECRET=
# Optional. Affiliate calls want a tracking id; "default" is accepted while
# you are only searching.
ALIEXPRESS_TRACKING_ID=
# Optional. Only set this to "md5" if hmac-sha256 signing is rejected —
# both schemes are accepted by the gateway and it declares which is in use.
ALIEXPRESS_SIGN_METHOD=

